        "original_id": "155df0bb-067f-5ea2-8dc1-cd10b447f214",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: National Maritime College of Ireland, Department of Defence, Cork City Council\n- Places: Ringaskiddy, County Cork, Ballincollig, Cork, Ireland\n- Topics: Education in Cork, county population\n\nFacts:\n- The National Maritime College of Ireland is situated on former Department of Defence land in Ringaskiddy, County Cork.\n- The National Maritime College of Ireland opened to students in 2004.\n- In 2016, County Cork had a population of 542,196, making it the third most populous county in Ireland.\n- The Cork city council area includes Ballincollig.\n- Education in Cork includes several third level colleges, including University College Cork, the Crawford College of Art and Design, and the National Maritime College of Ireland.",
